# /model as a user drives it: the selected row is visibly marked, ←/→
# changes effort, and picking a model closes the dialog with a
# confirmation. Scratch HOME: a pick writes the default model to user
# settings.
@real
@home scratch
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/ext-commands
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
TYPE /model
KEY enter
WAIT 1
SHOT picker-open
EXPECT /›\s+\d+\. \S+ ✓/
KEY right
WAIT 1
SHOT effort-changed
EXPECT /Effort set to (low|medium|high|xhigh|max) for this session/
EXPECT /effort  auto · low · medium · high · xhigh · max/
KEY down
WAIT 1
SHOT cursor-moved
EXPECT /›\s+\d+\. \S+\s{2,}/
KEY enter
WAIT 2
SHOT picked
EXPECT /Now on \S+ · \S+ tier · .* \(default for new sessions\)/
EXPECT_NOT /Select model/
